---
name: hybrid-assistant
description: A remote assistant answers known cases in Python and delegates judgment to an LLM.
engine: 0.2.0-lab.1
roles: [requester, assistant]
---
"""
The room enforces the conversation. A separate remote controller chooses whether
the Python program or LLM answers. Protocol validity does not prove answer quality.
"""
contract @30m => expired

"""
Ask one question at a time and evaluate the answer.
"""
role requester

"""
Answer exact common cases with the program. Delegate open-ended language and
judgment to the LLM; never guess that a fixed rule handles arbitrary English.
"""
role assistant

"""
One question. Ask the next only after its answer arrives.
"""
type question
  text: text(1..2000)

"""
Answer the question this reply names.
"""
type answer
  request: ref(question)
  text: text(1..4000)

"""
End the conversation; no further questions follow.
"""
type stop

"""
The requester asks the first question.
"""
state new
  """
  Ask a question. The assistant then owes one answer to it.
  """
  requester -> assistant: question() as request awaits answering
    """
    The assistant owns the deadline regardless of which implementation answers.
    """
    => answer(request=$request) & answered
     """
     No answer arrived within five minutes of the question.
     """
     | @5m & stalled

"""
The assistant answers the open question, by program or by LLM. At most ten
questions are asked.
"""
state answering max_entries 10 => exhausted

"""
Ask the next question, or stop.
"""
state answered
  requester -> assistant: question() as request => answering
  requester -> assistant: stop() => complete

"""
The requester stopped after the answers it needed. Their quality is still the requester's call.
"""
end complete

"""
An answer did not arrive in time. The requester decides whether to ask again elsewhere.
"""
end stalled

"""
An eleventh question was asked. Start a new session for more.
"""
end exhausted
